================================================================================
Why pdfcmprs is AGPL-3.0
================================================================================

Ghostscript, MuPDF, and CoherentPDF are distributed under the AGPL-3.0. Because
pdfcmprs ships and invokes them, the combined work must be offered under the
same terms. AGPL-3.0 section 13 additionally requires that users interacting
with the software over a network be offered the corresponding source; the
"Source" link in the site footer serves that purpose.

Note that all processing happens locally in the visitor's browser — no document
is uploaded to a server. The network clause applies to the software itself, not
to any document handling.

